./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3634:### Localhost 6789 Live Verification Plan For M1-M16
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3636:This plan creates the hard evidence needed to claim that the sixteen Authority
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3637:milestones were validated against a real local Python Proofbound Authority server at
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3638:`http://localhost:6789/`. It is a verification plan, not a second development
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3643:```text
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3644:1. don't optimize for the sake of optimization
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3646:3. only fix real correctness issues
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3647:4. preserve consistency of logic
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3650:The live verification must preserve two user-selected operating principles:
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3652:1. **Proofbound non-authority CLI.** The client is allowed to execute locally under
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3653:   local policy, with no Proofbound Authority server contact. This mode may produce
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3654:   local evidence, local validation, and local multi-host review, but it must not
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3655:   claim `authorityDone`, `fullAuthorityDone`, server receipt verification, or
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3656:   Python Authority evidence.
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3657:2. **Proofbound CLI + Proofbound Authority.** The client is still allowed to execute
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3658:   locally, but final Authority claims require server-verified evidence from the
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3659:   Python Proofbound Authority. In this mode the local runner executes provider /
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3660:   validation work, uploads signed evidence to `http://localhost:6789/`, requests
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3661:   or verifies native `gate_decision` receipts, and uses server-backed job /
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3662:   evidence / receipt / multi-host records before claiming Authority DONE.
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3664:These principles are not interchangeable. A non-authority pass protects local
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3665:developer ergonomics; an authority pass proves the local execution was backed by
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3666:server authority evidence. The final report must show both results separately.
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3668:The verification should use six verification milestones. Six is enough because
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3669:the original sixteen milestones are development outcomes; several can be proven
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3670:by the same live run and the same evidence chain. Splitting the verification into
