./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3743:| Verification milestone | Covers original milestones | Purpose | Required live evidence | Pass condition |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3745:| V1. Local Authority boot and trust pinning | M1, M3, M12 | Prove the real Python server is reachable on the local Authority default and exposes the expected metadata. | `curl -s http://localhost:6789/health`; `curl -s http://localhost:6789/v1/authority/policy`; captured `serverKey.publicKeyHex`; pinned key comparison; server startup command and env summary. | Server is reachable on `http://localhost:6789/`, policy parses, server key is pinned, and the run is not a stub or alternate-port substitute. |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3746:| V2. Cross-language signing and control plane | M1-M5 | Prove TypeScript and Python agree on signing, receipts, actor key registration, runner registration, heartbeat, claim, and release. | `npm run build`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-runner-contracts`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-runner-client`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-runner-events`; Python fixture/schema tests; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-live-python` against `http://localhost:6789/`. | Contract tests pass and live smoke outputs `passed: policy + control-plane`, not `SKIPPED`; release uses Python `release{runnerId,sessionId,reason}` and no `outcome`. |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3747:| V3. Stage B live execution loop | M6-M11 | Prove job schema, planned steps, provider execution, evidence upload, repair/stop policy, gate evaluation, receipt verification, and end-to-end Authority autopilot behavior while preserving local-only execution mode. | `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-job-loop`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-job-loop-live-smoke`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:evidence-upload-loop-smoke`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:evidence-live-wiring-smoke`; local/non-authority smoke proving zero server contact; live Authority evidence refs for run events, provider events, evidence upload, gate request, receipt verification, terminal status. | Non-authority execution can run locally with Authority flags false and no server contact; authority execution uploads evidence to the live server, gate receipt verification controls DONE, and failure paths release or block without dangling leases. |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3748:| V4. Stage C planner to Authority job | M13-M15 | Prove natural-language intake can create a Story draft, checklist, verification intent, Authority job, typed `plannedSteps[]`, and both non-authority and authority execution paths. | `npm --prefix packages/main run test:planner-unattended-smoke`; `npm --prefix packages/main run test:natural-language-to-done-smoke`; local planner run evidence with zero server contact; live job creation or live job-file equivalent bound to the same Story, planner digest, checklist digest, verification intent digest, and policy. | One-sentence and document-style requests produce non-placeholder Story/job plans; unsupported scope blocks; non-authority reports local-only status; authority DONE is claimed only after verified live receipt evidence. |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3749:| V5. Global Proofbound and deployment parity | M12 | Prove the globally installed `lattice` uses the same built code path and respects both non-authority and authority configuration. | Global `lattice check`; global local/non-authority smoke with no server contact; global `lattice authority` status/policy command where available; global `npm --prefix packages/main run test:authority-live-python` or equivalent global wrapper invocation; recorded binary realpath and package version. | Global `lattice` preserves local-only execution when non-authority is selected, and hits `http://localhost:6789/` with pinned-key verification only when authority mode is selected. |
./docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md:3750:| V6. Multi-host final certification and evidence closure | M16 plus final claim across M1-M15 | Prove final DONE is not a single-host overclaim. | Three bounded host-check waves before final DONE; each wave has at least two independent host verdicts, normally Codex CLI and Claude CLI, reviewing the same final anchors: commit/head, material hash, live smoke output, receipt refs, job/run ids, and evidence refs. Gemini may be added when available. Every wave prompt includes: `don't optimize for the sake of optimization`, `don't optimize arbitrarily`, `only fix real correctness issues`, and `preserve consistency of logic`. | Independent hosts return PASS in all three waves, or any real correctness BLOCK is repaired and the stale anchors are re-verified through fresh waves. Final claim explicitly states whether it is `localDone`, `authorityDone`, or `fullAuthorityDone`. |
